[core_mechanics.md] ## Proficiency Bonus: +3 for all player characters.
[fear_and_dread.md] ## The "Echo" (Seeing the Dead)
When a character sees an Echo (a lingering ghost-impression of the dead), they must make DC 10 Fear Save. Emmett is immune. Vera has advantage.
[investigation.md] ## Research (Books/Records)
Ravenmoor has a parish registry (at the chapel) and mine records (stolen from the Manor, now in the inn's back room).
- **Parish Registry**: DC 10 History to find relevant 
[investigation.md] ## Clue Tiers
Every location has tiered clues:
1. **Surface clue** — found on any successful check, or automatically if the party spends 10+ minutes.
2. **Hidden clue** — requires DC 13+ or specif
[core_mechanics.md] ## Contested Checks
When two characters oppose each other: both roll, highest wins. Ties go to the active party.

Casimir Voss is a deceased nobleman who owned Voss Manor, a large, crumbling mansion located on the outskirts of Ravenmoor village. The manor has a long history of supernatural activity and is rumored to be haunted. Casimir died under mysterious circumstances, and his death may be connected to the town's recent disturbing events. Voss Manor serves as a primary location in the Ravenmoor gothic horror TTRPG campaign. Here are some rules relevant to the session: The player characters have a proficiency bonus of +3 for all checks (core_mechanics.md, section 5). When a character sees an Echo (a lingering ghost-impression of the dead), they must make a DC 10 Fear Save. Emmett is immune, and Vera has advantage (fear_and_dread.md, section 7). Researching books or records can be done with varying degrees of success based on check results (investigation.md, section 6). Clues at locations have multiple tiers, with deeper clues requiring higher DCs (investigation.md, section 4). Contested checks are resolved by the highest roll winning, with ties going to the active party (core_mechanics.md, section 4).

